From: VirtualESP32 Android port
Subject: [PATCH] esp32_flash_enc: guard gcrypt.h include with CONFIG_GCRYPT

The encryption implementation already has an #ifdef CONFIG_GCRYPT branch
using QEMU's built-in qcrypto API as fallback, but the #include <gcrypt.h>
was unconditional, breaking builds without libgcrypt (e.g. Android/Bionic
ports that rely on the qcrypto fallback).

--- a/hw/misc/esp32_flash_enc.c
+++ b/hw/misc/esp32_flash_enc.c
@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@
  * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
  * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 or
  * (at your option) any later version.
  */
+#ifdef CONFIG_GCRYPT
 #include <gcrypt.h>
+#endif
 #include "qemu/osdep.h"
 #include "hw/hw.h"
 #include "hw/sysbus.h"
